<title>USA: ADVISORY - EIA delay next week, API, AGA on schedule.</title>
<headline>ADVISORY - EIA delay next week, API, AGA on schedule.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Energy Information Administration (EIA) said Friday that its weekly petroleum data would be delayed by one day next week until 0900 EST (1400 GMT) Thursday due to Monday's Veterans' Day holiday.</p>
<p>The American Petroleum Institute (API) said its weekly petroleum report will be issued as usual after 1630 EST (2130 GMT) on Tuesday, Nov. 12.</p>
<p>The American Gas Association (AGA) said its weekly underground storage data will be released as usual on Wednesday, Nov. 13, after 1600 EST (2100 GMT).</p>
</text>
